# Netlify does NOT automatically redirect the default *.netlify.app
# subdomain to a connected custom domain — both stay live and serve
# identical content unless a rule like this exists. This has to be a
# domain-specific rule (i.e. "from" includes the full https://host),
# and it must come BEFORE the SPA catch-all below, since Netlify
# processes _redirects rules top-to-bottom and uses the first match.
https://saicoaching.netlify.app/*  https://saicoaching.com/:splat  301!

# SPA fallback — every other path serves index.html so React Router
# (via the History API) can handle it client-side.
/*    /index.html   200
